h you should check local sanitation regulations first:\n* Wrap the hamster securely in paper towels or newspaper, place it inside a sealed plastic bag, and then place that inside a second bag (double-bagged).\n* Place the bag directly into your outside trash bin on collection day.\n\n### Immediate Steps (If you need time to decide)\nIf you need time to prepare a spot or wait for a vet clinic to open:\n1. Gently wrap your hamster in a clean paper towel or soft cloth.\n2. Place them inside a sealed plastic container or a zip-top bag.\n3. Keep the container in a cool, dry place. If you must wait more than a few hours, placing the container in a refrigerator or freezer (away from food) will preserve the body and prevent odor until you can proceed.",
