h.\n* **Preparation:** Wrap the hamster securely in several layers of newspaper or paper towels, place them inside a sealed plastic bag, and put that inside a second sealed bag. \n* **Timing:** Place the bag directly into your outside trash bin as close to collection day as possible to prevent odors and scavengers.\n\n***\n\n**A quick note on storage:** If you cannot bury or take your hamster to the vet immediately, place them in a sealed container and keep them in a cold place (a garage in winter, or wrapped securely in a freezer) to prevent natural decomposition until you are ready.",
